«
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  LgNrmQ
  @  Quantile: the X below which the probability is p.
  @  The exponential of the normal quantile of μl and σl: NormlQ does
  @  the work. p <= 0 gives 0, p >= 1 gives exp(μl+12·σl).
  @  Author & design          : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 3; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 3 ≠ THEN "LgNrmQ: needs 3 arguments" DoError END Explode Drop END
  → μlv σlv pv « μlv 0 + σlv 0 + pv 0 + → μl σl p «
    CASE
      p 0 ≤ THEN 0. END
      p 1 ≥ THEN 'EXP(μl+12*σl)' →Num END
      μl σl p ⓁNormlQ EXP
    END
    μlv σlv pv 3 →List Drop » »
»
